# NEARS-4208 window (d): SIMULATED tap intent (launcher intent with FCM-shaped extras + a pre-seeded plugin store record), NOT a delivered push. No FCM credential, no token, no push sent.
# method: firebase_messaging 16.7.0 FlutterFirebaseMessagingPlugin resolves a tap only if the intent carries google.message_id AND a RemoteMessage with that id exists in the in-memory map or the persisted store (SharedPreferences io.flutter.plugins.firebase.messaging, written by FlutterFirebaseMessagingReceiver on a real delivery). A bare 'am start' with extras finds no stored message -> getInitialMessage()/onMessageOpenedApp stay silent (explains the cycle-1 landing on home). QA seeded the store via run-as (debug APK) with records shaped like the backend payload (data + notification, acceptance_event) and launched: am start -n com.izzes.nears/.MainActivity --es google.message_id <id> --es google.sent_time 1792547000000 --es from 612345678 --es type order_status --es order_id <id> --es status confirmed [--es acceptance_event offered|held]
